================================================================================
Third-party components
================================================================================

This repository contains original code as well as model architectures that were
ported from or adapted from the projects listed below. Each upstream project is
governed by its own license; please consult the corresponding upstream
repository for its exact terms before reusing that code. The references below
are provided for attribution and reproducibility.

Skeleton-action model architectures
-----------------------------------
- CTR-GCN — Channel-wise Topology Refinement Graph Convolution (ICCV 2021)
  Upstream: https://github.com/Uason-Chen/CTR-GCN
  ( diema/models/ctrgcn/ )

- SkateFormer — Skeletal-Temporal Transformer (ECCV 2024)
  Upstream: https://github.com/KAIST-VICLab/SkateFormer
  ( diema/models/skateformer/ )

- ProtoGCN — Prototype-based Graph Convolution (CVPR 2025)
  Upstream: https://github.com/firework8/ProtoGCN
  ( diema/models/protogcn/ )

- ST-GCN / STGCN++ — Spatial-Temporal Graph Convolution
  Ported from an internal skeleton-action baseline maintained by the authors.
  ( diema/models/stgcn/ )

Sequence-model backbones (adapted from Kaggle competition solutions)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
- Conformer — Convolution-augmented Transformer (Gulati et al., INTERSPEECH 2020,
  https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.08100). Implementation adapted from the ASL
  Fingerspelling 11th-place solution by Baohao Liao and Shaomu Tan.
  Upstream: https://github.com/BaohaoLiao/aslfrv4
  ( diema/models/conformer/ )

- Squeezeformer (Kim et al., 2022, https://arxiv.org/abs/2206.00888) with
  rotary position embeddings (RoPE, https://arxiv.org/abs/2104.09864).
  Implementation adapted from the Kaggle ASL Fingerspelling 1st-place solution
  by Christof Henkel.
  Upstream: https://github.com/ChristofHenkel/kaggle-asl-fingerspelling-1st-place-solution
  ( diema/models/squeezeformer/ )

- Conv1D + Transformer hybrid — a faithful PyTorch port of the Kaggle ASL
  Signs 1st-place solution by hoyso48 (Hoyeol Sohn). This is the basis of our
  Region-Aware Conv-Transformer, the best single model in the ensemble.
  Upstream: https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/asl-signs/writeups/hoyeol-sohn-1st-place-solution-1dcnn-combined-with
  ( diema/models/conv1d_transformer/ )

- Keypoint Pool MLP — MLP-only two-stream (joint + bone) network with lateral
  connections, ported from the Kaggle ASL Signs 12th-place solution by
  DONJYARAHOI. Related paper: Two-Stream Network (https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.01367).
  Upstream: https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/asl-signs/writeups/donjyarahoi-12th-place-solution-mlp-based-structur
  ( diema/models/keypoint_pool_mlp/ )

- Skeleton augmentations (per-body-part sequence cutout, time-shift delta
  features) adapted from the Kaggle ASL Signs 8th-place solution by Darragh.
  ( diema/data/augmentations.py )

External-pretraining transfer backbones
---------------------------------------
- MotionBERT / MotionBERT-Lite (DSTformer) — used as a frozen feature extractor.
  Upstream: https://github.com/Walter0807/MotionBERT
  ( diema/models/motionbert/ )

- PoseC3D (ResNet3d-SlowOnly) — a clean-room, pure-PyTorch re-implementation of
  the PYSKL ResNet3dSlowOnly backbone, written to avoid the mmcv build
  dependency. No upstream weights are included.
  Upstream reference: https://github.com/kennymckormick/pyskl (PYSKL) and
  the MMAction2 project.
  ( diema/models/posec3d/ )

Architectural references (papers)
---------------------------------
- Structured Keypoint Pooling (https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.15270) additionally
  informs diema/models/keypoint_pool_mlp/.

